WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.689 --> 00:00:04.196
- The city dubbed America's
most dangerous had its

00:00:04.196 --> 00:00:05.212
highest murder rate ever.

00:00:05.212 --> 00:00:06.915
- Chicago is not the most dangerous city

00:00:06.915 --> 00:00:08.047
in America.

00:00:08.047 --> 00:00:10.280
Camden, New Jersey has that title

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:11.113
on a per capita basis.

00:00:11.113 --> 00:00:11.956
- I'm here in the park
side section of the city,

00:00:11.956 --> 00:00:14.445
an area that has been
labeled drug-infested

00:00:14.445 --> 00:00:15.278
and very dangerous.

00:00:15.278 --> 00:00:16.353
- Alarmingly, Camden's murder rate

00:00:16.353 --> 00:00:17.770
has more than doubled this year,

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:18.914
compared to last year from...

00:00:18.914 --> 00:00:19.747
(mumbling)

00:00:19.747 --> 00:00:23.055
- Life here in Camden is dangerous.

00:00:23.055 --> 00:00:25.555
Life here in Camden is deadly.

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:29.323
For every moment, for every second

00:00:29.323 --> 00:00:31.270
that the kids are out here playing,

00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:33.603
they're not getting shot at.

00:00:34.478 --> 00:00:36.260
For every second that they're here,

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:38.866
they're not witnessing
something that can get them hurt

00:00:38.866 --> 00:00:39.699
later on.

00:00:44.661 --> 00:00:47.541
The stakes are plain,
and right in front of us.

00:00:47.541 --> 00:00:50.296
For kids that aren't participating,

00:00:50.296 --> 00:00:52.322
you know they're hustling.

00:00:52.322 --> 00:00:55.122
For kids that are
participating in the league,

00:00:55.122 --> 00:00:56.205
they're safe.

00:01:09.743 --> 00:01:12.243
(dog barking)

00:01:16.638 --> 00:01:18.971
(sad music)

00:01:22.086 --> 00:01:22.975
- When I was a kid,

00:01:22.975 --> 00:01:26.782
the expectation was that
you would play baseball.

00:01:26.782 --> 00:01:29.867
That Pyne Poynt Park would
be a part of who you were

00:01:29.867 --> 00:01:31.284
and what you did.

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:36.331
But, by the time I'd become a teenager,

00:01:36.331 --> 00:01:39.339
there was this expectation that young men

00:01:39.339 --> 00:01:41.884
my age would become the bread earners

00:01:41.884 --> 00:01:44.384
by going out onto the corners.

00:01:47.034 --> 00:01:49.054
We were right in the
midst of the crack wars,

00:01:49.054 --> 00:01:50.679
and so, most of the young men

00:01:50.679 --> 00:01:53.768
that had once played baseball,
were now on the corners,

00:01:53.768 --> 00:01:55.518
and most of the people that had coached

00:01:55.518 --> 00:01:56.768
were now using.

00:01:58.767 --> 00:02:02.265
I'd dropped out of high
school, and began dealing drugs

00:02:02.265 --> 00:02:04.682
like many of my counterparts.

00:02:05.708 --> 00:02:08.303
I would eventually be
arrested and incarcerated

00:02:08.303 --> 00:02:10.655
and end up serving about 8 years

00:02:10.655 --> 00:02:12.905
in New Jersey State Prison.

00:02:14.437 --> 00:02:16.023
When I came home,

00:02:16.023 --> 00:02:20.190
it was truly with a sense that
I had to give something back.

00:02:22.074 --> 00:02:25.324
So I came up with the idea of baseball.

00:02:30.419 --> 00:02:32.776
Baseball hadn't been played in Camden

00:02:32.776 --> 00:02:35.128
for almost two decades,

00:02:35.128 --> 00:02:38.784
but I knew that there
was still a connection

00:02:38.784 --> 00:02:41.420
here in this neighborhood
and here in this city

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:42.670
with the sport.

00:02:45.402 --> 00:02:48.695
So I said look, if the
city's gonna be crazy,

00:02:48.695 --> 00:02:50.843
if the neighborhood's gonna be on fire,

00:02:50.843 --> 00:02:53.687
let's try to create
one safe place for kids

00:02:53.687 --> 00:02:55.104
in the neighborhood,

00:02:55.104 --> 00:02:57.937
and let's start a baseball league.

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:01.627
(phone ringing)

00:03:02.656 --> 00:03:03.950
Hey Jo, this is Brian,

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.994
just calling to see if
you had practice tonight

00:03:06.994 --> 00:03:08.576
with the softball.

00:03:08.576 --> 00:03:10.316
Matter of fact, I'm gonna
text all the other coaches

00:03:10.316 --> 00:03:12.300
and see who has practice tonight

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:14.824
and who still needs the catcher's gear.

00:03:14.824 --> 00:03:15.688
- Okay, cool.

00:03:15.688 --> 00:03:16.521
- Alright.

00:03:16.521 --> 00:03:17.354
- See you then.

00:03:17.354 --> 00:03:19.340
- Alright, see you then, thank you.

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:20.485
When I started coming out

00:03:20.485 --> 00:03:22.273
and saying hey we're gonna play baseball,

00:03:22.273 --> 00:03:26.251
I used to get people looking
at me like I was crazy.

00:03:26.251 --> 00:03:29.135
But I had to be that leader

00:03:29.135 --> 00:03:31.526
and in many instances I had to be fearless

00:03:31.526 --> 00:03:34.958
and be the one willing to go
up to ask the drug dealer,

00:03:34.958 --> 00:03:39.125
you know, between these hours,
would you mind not hustling?

00:03:39.581 --> 00:03:42.081
That's just what we had to do.

00:03:43.205 --> 00:03:47.020
And over time, the hustling
fell by the wayside,

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:49.937
and we became the norm in the park.

00:03:52.952 --> 00:03:56.079
- There you go, there you go.

00:03:56.079 --> 00:03:57.823
- Nice catch, college boy.

00:03:57.823 --> 00:04:00.383
- When we started, we ended
up with a hundred kids

00:04:00.383 --> 00:04:02.940
that year, and it blew our mind.

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:06.187
Today, we have over 650 kids playing,

00:04:06.187 --> 00:04:09.664
and that's kids playing from age 5

00:04:09.664 --> 00:04:11.747
all the way up to age 18.

00:04:14.288 --> 00:04:17.174
If you sat back and closed your eyes,

00:04:17.174 --> 00:04:19.360
you'd just hear the ping,

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:21.116
or the crack of the older kids

00:04:21.116 --> 00:04:23.340
when they use their wood bats.

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:25.902
The sound of the ball hitting leather,

00:04:25.902 --> 00:04:28.099
cleats scraping the gravel.

00:04:28.099 --> 00:04:30.336
Kids rattling on the fence, you know,

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:33.333
cheering go batter, batter, batter.

00:04:33.333 --> 00:04:37.073
People used to yell and scream
because something was wrong,

00:04:37.073 --> 00:04:38.787
and now people are yelling and screaming

00:04:38.787 --> 00:04:42.278
because something fantastic is happening.

00:04:42.278 --> 00:04:43.954
(cheering)

00:04:43.954 --> 00:04:45.491
Come game time,

00:04:45.491 --> 00:04:49.074
it's the most beautiful
thing in the world.

00:04:57.752 --> 00:04:59.142
So daddy's gonna teach you today

00:04:59.142 --> 00:05:03.162
how to hit off the batting tee, alright?

00:05:03.162 --> 00:05:05.999
As a father who tells
his daughter constantly

00:05:05.999 --> 00:05:07.717
that you can do anything that you want

00:05:07.717 --> 00:05:10.466
and be anything you want,
you know, you look up

00:05:10.466 --> 00:05:13.549
and you remember why you're doing it.

00:05:16.147 --> 00:05:18.426
Alright, good job.

00:05:18.426 --> 00:05:19.259
Ready?

00:05:19.259 --> 00:05:21.312
So much of our life in Camden

00:05:21.312 --> 00:05:23.981
and so much of our
lives in our urban cores

00:05:23.981 --> 00:05:27.398
is being hard, but kids for the few hours

00:05:29.368 --> 00:05:30.664
that they're here,

00:05:30.664 --> 00:05:32.543
they're just free to act out

00:05:32.543 --> 00:05:35.960
and become whatever hero they want to be.

00:05:37.402 --> 00:05:39.652
They're just free to laugh.

00:05:45.185 --> 00:05:47.712
It's not always gonna be easy,

00:05:47.712 --> 00:05:49.737
and there are forces at play

00:05:49.737 --> 00:05:53.147
that, they would love to see me fail.

00:05:53.147 --> 00:05:55.101
I have to continue to dig deep

00:05:55.101 --> 00:05:59.268
and put the grind in because
I just know I gotta do it.

00:06:01.676 --> 00:06:02.693
Come on.

00:06:02.693 --> 00:06:03.526
Good.

00:06:03.526 --> 00:06:07.476
If I don't do it, no
one else is gonna do it.

00:06:07.476 --> 00:06:09.144
You know I tell myself
there's plenty of time

00:06:09.144 --> 00:06:10.977
to rest when I'm dead.

00:06:11.947 --> 00:06:12.780
Until then,

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:15.697
I'm gonna live life to the fullest.

